            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/worker.cpp",
                    "line": 462,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jinu Joy Thomas",
                        "email": "jinu.joy.thomas@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jinuthomas"
                    },
                    "message": "do we need to throw here or try the remaining so that if the failure happened after it was removed and before returning we could still try and create a new one , this will allow the below check of exists to throw"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/worker.cpp",
                    "line": 462,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "As we are not aware of internals of the remove API its difficult to say if there can be any scenario where removal was done but still there is an exception.\nFrom documentation we can conclude that it will return false when API fails either with or without exception. It\u2019s difficult to say where the exception occurred before or after removal.\nFor us, the caller, call to remove failed so calling create after this does not make any sense is what I think."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/worker.cpp",
                    "line": 462,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jinu Joy Thomas",
                        "email": "jinu.joy.thomas@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jinuthomas"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
            ],
